id: F31
target: src/sello/field.nim
desc: feCMove: the value barrier dropped from the mask construction, 'let mask = valueBarrier32(-int32(b))' -> 'let mask = -int32(b)' (RFC-005 fix-slice 22a's own remedy, removed).
status: equivalent (retired -- excluded from the active catalog, not counted in the kill rate)
note: Verified empirically. The mutated line computes the IDENTICAL int32 value on every real execution (valueBarrier32 is the identity function -- see private/ct.nim's own doc comment) -- there is no arithmetic difference for any correctness-oriented test to observe. Applied to a scratch copy of the tree and run against the FULL scripts/test.sh battery (both the unit + Wycheproof + libsodium-differential suite and all six proptest property suites, gcc backend, 20 file(s) total): SURVIVED, zero failures (confirmed this slice, real container run). The one instrument that WOULD kill this mutant is the clang leg of the taint CT harness (taint-ct-linux-amd64-clang, RFC-005 slice 22/22a): dropping valueBarrier32 reopens exactly the defect fix-slice 22a closed -- clang's -O3 re-proves mask is confined to {0, -1} (bool-derived) and re-synthesizes the masked-select loop into a branch on the secret bit, the same finding recorded in this project's handoff doc and CLAUDE.md's private/ct.nim entry (confirmed directly: this exact removal is how the pre-22a source read, and it reproduced 4348 memcheck errors from 100 contexts on target_sign both locally and on real hosted CI). tests/mutation/'s own harness (scripts/mutation.sh) never runs under valgrind/taint and has no clang leg, so it structurally cannot distinguish this mutant from the fixed source -- the identical "equivalent under this instrument, killed only by a different instrument this catalog doesn't drive" situation the F05/H07 precedents established, not a defect in either instrument. Reported per the catalog's own guidance (a survivor genuinely equivalent under the instrument it was scored against is retired with recorded evidence, not forced through an artificial assertion the unit suite has no organic reason to make).
====OLD====
  let mask = valueBarrier32(-int32(b))
====NEW====
  let mask = -int32(b)
====END====
